Laboratory1: You can find abandoned laboratories scattered around the world.
Laboratory2: You can easily turn a laboratory into apartments, but the monsters lurking there will not like it.
Laboratory3: Each laboratory has a generator room in the basement. Try flipping the power switch in there.
Laboratory4: You can right-click an elevator to move to a different floor.
WhiteTail1: If you defeat enough latex beasts, you might invoke the wrath of a very fast monster.
Puro1: A friendly black goo can move in if you manage to slay a very fast monster.
WolfKing1: You may encounter the leader of a wolf pack in a room filled with black goo.
EvolutionTip1: Monsters grow bigger and stronger every time a boss is defeated.
RottenOrange1: Carrying a rotten orange is enough to see strange things.
DrK1: A scientist can move in who sells useful potions for your adventures.
Prototype1: A robot can move in who sells fruit for dishes and herbs for potions.
Prototype2: If you need more wood you can let the gardening robot walk near saplings to make them grow into trees faster.
Rain1: Aquatic beasts appear more often during rain.
Windy1: Flying beasts appear more often on windy days.
StrongLatex1: You can encounter strong monsters near labs in the crimson and corruption, and rarely in other places.
Syringe1: Syringes let you transform into different creatures.
